# This site has one generated, public JSON input that must remain in Railway
# upload bundles.
#
# History worth keeping: the root repo used to ignore every directory named
# `data/` (unanchored), and these negations were written to work around it.
# They never actually worked — git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation for a path *inside* one can never fire.
# public/data/buildings.json survived purely because it was already tracked,
# and ignore rules do not apply to tracked files; a `git rm --cached` or a
# regeneration into a fresh clone would have silently lost it.
# The root rule was anchored to `/data/` on 2026-08-07, which both removes the
# need for this workaround and makes it functional for the first time.
# Harmless to keep as belt-and-braces.
!public/data/
!public/data/**
